# Replication Evidence Gate

- Treat `docs/FINAL_BEHAVIOR_SPEC.md` as the behavior contract.
- Read `docs/REPLICATION_AUDIT.md` before designing or coding the EA.
- Never claim a video reveals hidden entry logic, trader instinct, or long-term
  profitability when it does not.
- “100% compliant” means every approved deterministic rule is implemented and
  tested; it never means guaranteed profits or identical future trades.
- Keep observed facts, assumptions, unknowns, and our safety modifications
  explicitly separated.
- No full EA implementation until the pre-code acceptance gate is approved.
- Every decision engine must emit testable reason codes and telemetry.
- Any feature not supported by evidence starts disabled.
- RiskGovernor may always veto an otherwise valid signal.
- For $10 equity, skip trades whose broker-minimum volume exceeds the risk budget.

## Forbidden shortcuts

- Do not invent a secret indicator or call arbitrary thresholds “instinct.”
- Do not use martingale, recovery grids, unlimited layers, or add to losers.
- Do not optimize on a single highlight/session and call it profitable.
- Do not hide losing scenarios or execution costs in validation reports.
